Why this revision. Docking is not in Dear ImGui's release branch: the
release headers carry the marker `#ifdef IMGUI_HAS_DOCK` with the
comment that its contents are filled in on the `docking` branch, and
nothing fills it. The viewer was written against release 1.90.1, so
this is the docking branch at the same release: the only thing that
changes from what the viewer built against before is docking itself.
The vendored plotting library beside this one is pinned to a revision
of its own and was written against the same Dear ImGui release.

What was taken and what was left. The library's four source files and
its headers, the three bundled text and packing headers it includes,
and the two backends the viewer uses: GLFW for the window and OpenGL 3
for the renderer, with the loader header that second one includes.
Left behind: the demo source, the documentation tree, the examples,
the miscellaneous helpers, and the seventeen backends for windowing
and rendering paths this viewer does not take.

Nothing here is modified. An update is a fresh copy at a new named
revision, with this file rewritten to name it.
